From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ARM: configs: gts28ltexx: the network options Android's netd
 needs

Inside the Waydroid container Android's netd gives each network its own
routing table and steers traffic with fwmarks: without policy routing
(IP_MULTIPLE_TABLES) "ip rule" is refused, the network gets an address but
no route out and no resolver, and Google's services cannot even check in
("Unable to resolve host"). Adds policy routing for IPv4 and IPv6, the
mark and connmark matches and targets, the raw, security and IPv6 mangle
and NAT tables, the netlink queue and log, and the traffic control pieces
netd configures (HTB, ingress, u32 and BPF classifiers, IFB).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig | 71 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 71 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig b/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig
index 5d04c41a9..e2fd6b9ae 100644
--- a/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_defconfig
@@ -385,3 +385,74 @@ CONFIG_SQUASHFS_XZ=y
 CONFIG_TUN=y
 CONFIG_VLAN_8021Q=y
 CONFIG_BRIDGE_VLAN_FILTERING=y
+
+# Android's own network stack inside the Waydroid container: netd routes each
+# network through its own table (policy routing, fwmarks) and builds its
+# firewall, accounting and tethering chains from these matches and targets;
+# without them the container gets an address but no route out and no DNS.
+CONFIG_IP_ADVANCED_ROUTER=y
+CONFIG_IP_MULTIPLE_TABLES=y
+CONFIG_IPV6_ROUTER_PREF=y
+CONFIG_IPV6_ROUTE_INFO=y
+CONFIG_IPV6_OPTIMISTIC_DAD=y
+CONFIG_IPV6_MULTIPLE_TABLES=y
+CONFIG_INET_ESP=y
+CONFIG_INET6_ESP=y
+CONFIG_INET_UDP_DIAG=y
+CONFIG_INET_DIAG_DESTROY=y
+CONFIG_UNIX_DIAG=y
+CONFIG_PACKET_DIAG=y
+CONFIG_XFRM_USER=y
+CONFIG_NF_CONNTRACK_MARK=y
+CONFIG_NF_CT_NETLINK=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_NETLINK_QUEUE=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_NETLINK_LOG=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MARK=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_CONNMARK=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_TARGET_CLASSIFY=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_TARGET_CONNMARK=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_TARGET_CT=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_TARGET_IDLETIMER=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_TARGET_MARK=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_TARGET_NFLOG=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_TARGET_NFQUEUE=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_TARGET_TPROXY=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_TARGET_TCPMSS=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_BPF=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_CONNMARK=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_HELPER=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_IPRANGE=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_LENGTH=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_MAC=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_MARK=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_PKTTYPE=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_POLICY=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_QUOTA=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_SOCKET=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_STATISTIC=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_STRING=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_TIME=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_U32=y
+CONFIG_IP_NF_MATCH_RPFILTER=y
+CONFIG_IP_NF_MATCH_TTL=y
+CONFIG_IP_NF_RAW=y
+CONFIG_IP_NF_SECURITY=y
+CONFIG_IP_NF_ARPTABLES=y
+CONFIG_IP_NF_ARPFILTER=y
+CONFIG_IP_NF_ARP_MANGLE=y
+CONFIG_IP6_NF_MATCH_RPFILTER=y
+CONFIG_IP6_NF_MANGLE=y
+CONFIG_IP6_NF_RAW=y
+CONFIG_IP6_NF_NAT=y
+CONFIG_IP6_NF_TARGET_MASQUERADE=y
+CONFIG_NET_SCHED=y
+CONFIG_NET_SCH_HTB=y
+CONFIG_NET_SCH_INGRESS=y
+CONFIG_NET_CLS_U32=y
+CONFIG_NET_CLS_BPF=y
+CONFIG_NET_CLS_ACT=y
+CONFIG_NET_ACT_POLICE=y
+CONFIG_NET_ACT_GACT=y
+CONFIG_NET_ACT_MIRRED=y
+CONFIG_NET_ACT_BPF=y
+CONFIG_IFB=y
